-- and the distribution of a sum of uniforms, from an independent Python
-- oracle: clipped areas inside nested adaptive Gauss-Kronrod in quantile
-- space, and a Monte Carlo of the same priors (10000000 draws, seed 20261112).
-- Reference error bound: 1e-8 of each probability; largest quadrature error
-- estimate in this run: 1.97e-10 of the value. Largest gap between the two
-- oracle methods: 1.39 standard errors. selection.ail must agree with the
-- quadrature to 1e-8 of the value and with the Monte Carlo within 3 standard errors.
